Dear OCaml users,=20

We have the pleasure of celebrating the birthdays of Marie Sk=C5=82odowska-=
Curie and=20
Lise Meitner by announcing the release of OCaml version 4.14.5.=20

This release is a safe collection of six security fixes, one pattern-matchi=
ng=20
miscompilation fix, and one configuration fix for the newest version of mac=
OS.=20
See the full Changes list below.=20

If we are using any previous 4.14 version of OCaml, we are advising you to=
=20
switch to this new version.=20

### Evaluating the end of the active maintenance of OCaml 4.14=20

As an important announcement, in January 2027, we will start evaluating if =
it=20
would be reasonable to stop the active maintenance of the 4.14 branch betwe=
en=20
January and June 2027, taking in account that maintaining 4.14 is becoming =
more=20
arduous each passing year.=20

If this evaluation does not reveal any major issues, we would stop the acti=
ve=20
maintenance of OCaml 4.14 between June 2027 and the end of 2027. OCaml 4.14=
=20
would still be available, and we would still try to keep the branch compati=
ble=20
with newer OSs and C compilers on a best effort basis.=20

In the meanwhile, do not hesitate to report any bugs on the OCaml issue tra=
cker=20
(https://github.com/ocaml/ocaml/issues).=20

Happy hacking,=20
Florian Angeletti for the OCaml team.=20


Installation Instructions=20
-------------------------=20

The base compiler can be installed as an opam switch with the following=20
commands:=20

opam update=20
opam switch create 4.14.5=20

The source code for the release candidate is also directly available on:=20
* GitHub: https://github.com/ocaml/ocaml/archive/4.14.5.tar.gz=20
* Inria archive: https://caml.inria.fr/pub/distrib/ocaml-4.14/ocaml-4.14.5.=
tar.gz=20


Changes in OCaml 4.14.5 (6 November 2026)=20
--------------------------------------=20
### Bug fixes:=20

- 15019(https://github.com/ocaml/ocaml/issues/15019), 15030(https://github.=
com/ocaml/ocaml/issues/15030), OSEC-2026-18(https://osv.dev/vulnerability/O=
SEC-2026-18): `Marshal.from_{string,bytes}`: guard against=20
overflow in the computation of the total data length.=20
(Xavier Leroy, report by Akshay Singh, review by Nicol=C3=A1s Ojeda B=C3=A4=
r=20
and Antonin D=C3=A9cimo)=20

- 15113(https://github.com/ocaml/ocaml/issues/15113), OSEC-2026-21(https://=
osv.dev/vulnerability/OSEC-2026-21): `Str.string_partial_match`: make sure =
captured groups=20
are valid.=20
(Xavier Leroy, review by Nicol=C3=A1s Ojeda B=C3=A4r and Edwin T=C3=B6r=C3=
=B6k)=20

- 15112(https://github.com/ocaml/ocaml/issues/15112), OSEC-2026-22(https://=
osv.dev/vulnerability/OSEC-2026-22): `Unix.map_file`: protect against overf=
low=20
when computing the data size.=20
(Xavier Leroy and Nicol=C3=A1s Ojeda B=C3=A4r, review by Nicol=C3=A1s Ojeda=
 B=C3=A4r=20
and Edwin T=C3=B6r=C3=B6k)=20

- 15115(https://github.com/ocaml/ocaml/issues/15115), OSEC-2026-23(https://=
osv.dev/vulnerability/OSEC-2026-23): Fix multiple issues in demarshaling=20
(`Marshal.from_{channel,string,bytes}`)=20
(Xavier Leroy, review by Nicol=C3=A1s Ojeda B=C3=A4r)=20

- 15133(https://github.com/ocaml/ocaml/issues/15133), OSEC 2026-24(https://=
osv.dev/vulnerability/OSEC-2026-24): Multiple issues in command quoting on =
Windows=20
(Xavier Leroy and Nicol=C3=A1s Ojeda B=C3=A4r, review by Nicol=C3=A1s Ojeda=
 B=C3=A4r)=20

- 15233(https://github.com/ocaml/ocaml/issues/15233), OSEC-2026-30(https://=
osv.dev/vulnerability/OSEC-2026-30): ensure that ephemeron marking follows =
Infix pointers.=20
(Gabriel Scherer, review by Florian Angeletti)=20

- 15185(https://github.com/ocaml/ocaml/issues/15185), 15187(https://github.=
com/ocaml/ocaml/issues/15187): fix a pattern-matching miscompilation on cer=
tain=20
combinations of immediate ranges and redundant patterns=20
(Gabriel Scherer, report by Alperer Kele=C5=9F,=20
review by Vincent Laviron and Florian Angeletti)=20

- 15067(https://github.com/ocaml/ocaml/issues/15067), 15071(https://github.=
com/ocaml/ocaml/issues/15071): Fix detection of functions available in the =
future on macOS.=20
(Antonin D=C3=A9cimo, review by Nicol=C3=A1s Ojeda B=C3=A4r and Damien Doli=
gez)=20


### Internal tools:=20

- 11100(https://github.com/ocaml/ocaml/issues/11100): Fix ocamltest to make=
 sure failed tests are not counted as=20
"unexpected error".=20
(Damien Doligez, review by S=C3=A9bastien Hinderer)=20


